{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "kanban-muse-issue-11-cold-generated-host-targets-1788055517675", :event/time "2026-08-30T02:05:17.675Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "muse-issue-11-cold-generated-host-targets", :text "Exact-head review finding accepted (PR #14 comment 3888218476; reviewed commit 35d0222261fc7a216b5c3cf0ee38a9274810d2ce): atomic rename at the repository pathname would replace a supported .mcp.json symlink rather than update its shared target. Superseding correction: atomic publication resolves an existing symlink to its ultimate target, creates the staging file in that target directory, and renames over the target; the repository symlink remains unchanged. The same helper covers the ownership sidecar and rollback. CI now routes both state files through external symlinks and requires unchanged link text plus replaced target inodes. Local successful publication and injected-failure rollback preserve both symlinks and exact target bytes; shell, workflow, and diff checks pass. The card remains testing pending the next immutable-head hosted gates and reviews.", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1788055517672-0.l65qttsebzicvgay4bd", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "a47b30ba-f6c9-4300-96f6-1598f124b246"}
{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "kanban-muse-issue-11-cold-generated-host-targets-1788056310532", :event/time "2026-08-30T02:18:30.532Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "muse-issue-11-cold-generated-host-targets", :text "Exact-head review findings accepted (PR #14 comments 3888234413 and 3888234414; reviewed commit ec8395f745783dd1b5ccebda7ab609b2bd366f0b): atomic staging inherited mktemp mode 0600 instead of the existing destination's shared permissions, and rollback restored registry before ownership, making an interrupted partial rollback unsafe after a rename. Superseding correction: staged files copy an existing target's uid, gid, and permission bits, or use 0666 masked by the process umask for a new destination. Rollback restores/removes ownership first and restores the registry only if that succeeds, preserving the safe new-registry/old-ownership intermediate order. CI asserts 0640/0660 symlink-target modes and injects ownership-restore failure after a retired Claude identity, requiring registry rollback to be skipped and the canonical new registry/ownership pair to remain. Local permissions, exact rollback order, injected restore failure, shell, workflow, and diff checks pass; the card remains testing pending the next immutable-head hosted gates and reviews.", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1788056310527-0.suys5bx2cysnfckajcj", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "a1a2bb84-395c-49db-b5d0-1d549f4fded9"}
{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "kanban-muse-issue-11-cold-generated-host-targets-1788057209837", :event/time "2026-08-30T02:33:29.837Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "muse-issue-11-cold-generated-host-targets", :text "Exact-head review findings accepted (PR #14 comments 3888254123 and 3888254126; reviewed commit 52428076c7d138c85f2f58fae38b2fe5d474107f): the wrapper still hard-coded .mcp.json despite configurable :publish :mcp-config, and metadata preservation could fail late by attempting cross-UID chown on a shared destination. Superseding correction: each requested MCP target exposes its canonical configured destination; the wrapper resolves all requested paths under the lock before snapshot/build, rejects divergent multi-target destinations, publishes to that path, and scopes non-default ownership state alongside it. Existing destinations and resolved symlink targets must pass current-UID, available-group, and directory-write preflight before any generator or Shadow release; atomic publication refuses an ownership change after preflight rather than attempting cross-user chown. CI changes the generic target to an absolute non-default destination, requires output/ownership there, and proves the default registry remains byte-identical. Local configured-destination, divergent-request fail-before-generation, shell, workflow, Clojure lint, and diff checks pass; the card remains testing pending the next immutable-head hosted gates and reviews.", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1788057209833-0.2s0aqpfxgmjl828mawz", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "a84fc34a-498f-4018-a864-d0f564fb8e00"}
{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "kanban-muse-issue-11-cold-generated-host-targets-1788058233060", :event/time "2026-08-30T02:50:33.060Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "muse-issue-11-cold-generated-host-targets", :text "Exact-head review findings accepted and corrected (PR #14 comments 3888279728 and 3888279731; reviewed commit 1a01af5903d3cb00e199816df8d0dd1c0ce35939), together with CodeRabbit's owner-file startup-window nitpick: a repository-local lock did not serialize separate checkouts sharing one external MCP destination, and atomic replacement preserved only basic uid/gid/mode rather than named POSIX ACLs. Superseding correction: resolve the configured registry to its canonical ultimate destination before lock acquisition and place the ownership directory beside that destination, so absolute and symlink aliases across checkouts contend on one lock. Existing destination metadata is copied to the staged inode with GNU cp --attributes-only --preserve=all before rename, preserving POSIX ACLs and other access metadata; CI snapshots raw registry and ownership ACL xattrs and requires exact bytes after both replacements. Lock contention now retries the owner read briefly before classifying a lock invalid, and the hosted gate pins a live lock at a non-default destination and requires failure before generation. Local destination-lock, symlink-alias contention, mode-preservation, shell, workflow, and diff checks pass; the card remains testing pending the corrected immutable-head hosted gates and reviews.", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1788058233057-0.gvuvdpz28yfxxfyxnjp", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "bebcc7b6-ed40-48e8-9194-0983ae18e992"}
{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "kanban-muse-issue-11-cold-generated-host-targets-1788058935568", :event/time "2026-08-30T03:02:15.568Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "muse-issue-11-cold-generated-host-targets", :text "Exact-head review findings accepted and corrected (PR #14 comments 3888309256 and 3888309260; reviewed commit 7f439adc00e6b5951bbf8e637d40dcad5b44af6f): canonical locking alone left alias-specific ownership sidecars, and raw target path comparison rejected equivalent relative, absolute, or symlink spellings before canonicalization. Superseding correction: canonicalize every requested target destination independently before comparing them, use the single resolved registry identity for publication, and derive both the ownership sidecar and lock from that identity. The canonical repository .mcp.json retains its compatibility sidecar/lock names; any external or symlink-resolved registry uses one sidecar and lock beside the ultimate target, so all protected writers read the same target-to-registration state. CI routes the repository registry through an external symlink whose canonical sidecar is shared, and proves an all-target request with relative and absolute spellings reaches the active canonical lock rather than a false divergence. Local canonical-sidecar publication, equivalent symlink/direct alias contention, shell, workflow, and diff checks pass; the card remains testing pending the next corrected immutable-head hosted gates and reviews.", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1788058935564-0.snd9u4azzqmlxuqa55a", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "733cd6d4-62e0-4374-9e94-b077ed6dcae8"}
